{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QjEWKmiS4ZvjxyMnHg2cfM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system for J.C. Liechty. Grounded summary:\n\n**What it is**\n- A single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), stdlib-only Python app that turns plain markdown files into the source of truth for tasks, projects, and notes â€” no database, no syncing, no external dependencies (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n- It ships as a **persistent local web server** (`anchor_gui.py`, bound to `http://localhost:8777`) run as the Windows NSSM service `anchor`, plus a CLI mirror (`anchor.py`).\n\n**What it does (core productivity layer)**\n- Renders an interactive browser dashboard over markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files) where you check tasks done, add tasks, capture ideas â€” all written straight back to markdown and logged.\n- Manages a full task lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, across domains (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n- Runs a daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, and writes a health report.\n\n**What it does (R&D control surface â€” the bulk of recent work)**\n- Layers a per-project \"cockpit\" that drives the **trio** workflow (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, isolated, server-side sessions.\n- Each project lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) shows its most-recent session as a tile with an honest status light; clicking expands an **inline panel** with a cached, grounded summary on top and a **real, resizable ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js) below.\n- Opening a session \"feels like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session\" â€” the lane's skill auto-loads **once**, greets once, then behaves normally (the fix for the old repeating-prompt bug).\n- Supporting machinery: git-worktree-per-session isolation, a durable session registry, cached/validated session+project summaries, stage handoffs, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), per-project cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool/service/program/doc).\n\n**What it ships**\n- Four built + merged-to-master iterations of that surface: v2 (sessions/summaries/grass/terminal), v3 \"Mission Control\" (ConPTY, worktrees, window manager, GWL branding), and v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (one terminal substrate, engine toggle, inline panels, rollups, flat rows) â€” the latter merged 2026-06-13 (637 tests passing).\n- Branded as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\", with a vendored brand mark serving as the favicon.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: the above is drawn from the project's own `CLAUDE.md` and frozen plan docs, which are the project's self-description rather than an independent audit of the running code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fb5b19a-acf7-411f-bf40-dd981756283f","uuid":"2add19d8-97f9-40de-9293-c29b27dab01d","request_id":"req_011Cc1fPCx6Jf8vcMPqpY6Eo"}
